1
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:47,979
[When I Meet The Moon]

2
00:01:48,110 --> 00:01:51,100
[Episode 4]

3
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:05,900
This Little Kid does talk nonsense
all the time,

4
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:08,300
but he's quite reliable when he's working.

5
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:15,780
Smells so good.

6
00:02:16,190 --> 00:02:17,320
It'll be ready soon.

7
00:02:24,130 --> 00:02:24,930
Tangy!

8
00:02:25,250 --> 00:02:27,250
What kind of cursed cuisine is this?

9
00:02:31,180 --> 00:02:33,370
I was just trying to expand

10
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,950
our guesthouse's menu.

11
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:36,710
Just leave it to me.

12
00:02:36,870 --> 00:02:39,120
Why don't you go help Lili?

13
00:02:39,470 --> 00:02:40,990
I don't want anyone to get food poisoning

14
00:02:40,990 --> 00:02:42,280
before we even open.

15
00:02:42,310 --> 00:02:43,680
Go help her. Go ahead.

16
00:02:46,430 --> 00:02:47,760
What are you staring at?

17
00:02:48,790 --> 00:02:49,990
You were spacing out.

18
00:02:52,190 --> 00:02:53,460
The meat is burnt!

19
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:55,700
Well...

20
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:57,430
I... I was just thinking about something

21
00:02:57,430 --> 00:02:58,760
and zoning out for a bit.

22
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,940
Thinking about your sweetheart?

23
00:03:02,930 --> 00:03:03,930
What sweetheart?

24
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:07,900
Tang Lin said
she wanted some sweetheart cakes.

25
00:03:15,090 --> 00:03:16,400
Your sweetheart is here.

26
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:16,910
Uncle!

27
00:03:16,910 --> 00:03:18,640
Remember to say hi to him later.

28
00:03:24,030 --> 00:03:25,490
You even brought red wine?

29
00:03:37,310 --> 00:03:38,060
Well,

30
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:38,860
Xia,

31
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:40,090
w-we don't have enough food.

32
00:03:40,090 --> 00:03:41,350
I'll chop up some more.

33
00:03:58,370 --> 00:03:59,180
Here, Uncle.

34
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:01,410
Thanks,

35
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,280
Lili.

36
00:04:02,810 --> 00:04:03,620
Thank you.

37
00:04:05,410 --> 00:04:06,340
What about mine?

38
00:04:06,650 --> 00:04:08,470
I don't even have enough for myself.

39
00:04:08,470 --> 00:04:09,650
Don't you still have some more?

40
00:04:09,650 --> 00:04:10,620
Give me one.

41
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:13,510
I don't have enough for myself.

42
00:04:16,010 --> 00:04:16,810
Tangy,

43
00:04:17,250 --> 00:04:18,360
don't stoop to the level

44
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,120
of an ill-mannered brat.

45
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,850
Take this freshly grilled one.

46
00:04:21,870 --> 00:04:23,270
Xia, you're the best.

47
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:25,270
How can we have a barbecue without cola?

48
00:04:25,270 --> 00:04:26,470
I'll fetch some cola.

49
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:29,980
There's

50
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:31,160
a freshly made crepe roll in the fridge.

51
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,270
Can you get it for me?

52
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:32,980
Sure.

53
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,000
Make way.

54
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:44,120
Old Auntie,

55
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,680
first come, first served.

56
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,340
Can't you wait until I'm done?

57
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:49,159
Move away.

58
00:05:17,850 --> 00:05:19,980
Thank goodness the cola didn't spill.

59
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:44,860
Lili!

60
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:47,659
Your milk.

61
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,470
Thanks.

62
00:05:54,250 --> 00:05:55,850
My uncle doesn't drink cola.

63
00:05:56,159 --> 00:05:56,770
Li.

64
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:11,010
Um,

65
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:13,690
why do Fu Zhengchu and Xia

66
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:15,430
have different surnames?

67
00:06:15,890 --> 00:06:17,820
Aren't they biological siblings?

68
00:06:18,870 --> 00:06:21,000
Fu Zhengchu took my sister's surname.

69
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:22,980
Xia Congsheng

70
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:25,560
was supposed
to take my sister's surname, too.

71
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:26,720
Then was Fu Zhengchu

72
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:28,750
supposed to take his dad's surname?

73
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:29,430
Nope.

74
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:33,180
My brother-in-law is quite henpecked.

75
00:06:33,370 --> 00:06:34,510
What about you?

76
00:06:37,870 --> 00:06:38,480
Well,

77
00:06:38,570 --> 00:06:41,300
I was asking
if you're also afraid of your sister,

78
00:06:41,950 --> 00:06:44,980
not if you're afraid of... your wife.

79
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:49,000
Yun Li,

80
00:06:49,330 --> 00:06:51,390
what nonsense are you talking about?

81
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,200
By the way.

82
00:06:53,490 --> 00:06:55,740
What's your name?

83
00:06:56,590 --> 00:06:57,200
Yun Li.

84
00:06:58,060 --> 00:06:59,630
Yun Li... Li.

85
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:12,070
He didn't mention the meme.

86
00:07:12,420 --> 00:07:14,480
I'll just pretend it never happened.

87
00:07:19,250 --> 00:07:20,060
Come on.

88
00:07:21,010 --> 00:07:21,810
Lili,

89
00:07:22,450 --> 00:07:23,810
are you going to register tomorrow?

90
00:07:23,810 --> 00:07:24,620
Yep.

91
00:07:24,950 --> 00:07:26,360
Why don't you go with us?

92
00:07:27,660 --> 00:07:28,860
No need to trouble you.

93
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:29,860
I-I can just go

94
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:30,880
with Tangy.

95
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:31,950
It's no trouble.

96
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:33,950
My uncle is driving us there anyway.

97
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:36,610
Is that okay, Uncle?

98
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:38,420
Mm.

99
00:07:47,159 --> 00:07:47,950
Lili,

100
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:49,040
what's your major?

101
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:50,360
Automation.

102
00:07:51,420 --> 00:07:52,220
How about this?

103
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:53,570
You and my uncle may wait in the car.

104
00:07:53,570 --> 00:07:54,370
It's scorching hot outside.

105
00:07:54,370 --> 00:07:55,159
Let me go check where

106
00:07:55,159 --> 00:07:55,950
you need to register.

107
00:07:55,950 --> 00:07:56,420
It's fine.

108
00:07:56,420 --> 00:07:57,570
I can go by myself.

109
00:07:57,570 --> 00:07:58,450
You're not familiar with the campus.

110
00:07:58,450 --> 00:07:59,370
It'll be more trouble

111
00:07:59,370 --> 00:08:00,510
if you get lost.

112
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,070
I'm off, Uncle.

113
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:03,510
Thanks.

114
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:05,420
Bye-bye.

115
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:22,280
Thank you for giving us a lift...

116
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:24,950
Uncle.

117
00:08:31,150 --> 00:08:31,650
Mm.

118
00:08:36,270 --> 00:08:37,860
I've actually been looking for

119
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:39,220
an internship recently.

120
00:08:39,220 --> 00:08:40,400
Xia and Tangy

121
00:08:40,429 --> 00:08:41,809
helped me pick a few,

122
00:08:42,669 --> 00:08:43,480
but I'm still not sure

123
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:45,140
which one to send my resume to.

124
00:08:45,510 --> 00:08:47,210
Could you help me take a look?

125
00:08:48,630 --> 00:08:49,130
Mm.

126
00:08:55,390 --> 00:08:57,580
Why did I bring this up?

127
00:08:57,580 --> 00:08:59,290
I should've just asked him if he

128
00:08:59,290 --> 00:09:00,530
minds me going to EAW.

129
00:09:00,530 --> 00:09:01,990
That would be much easier!

130
00:09:05,830 --> 00:09:06,620
If...

131
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:07,200
EAW

132
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:08,200
suits you better.

133
00:09:11,750 --> 00:09:12,270
Here.

134
00:09:13,690 --> 00:09:14,550
Thank you.

135
00:09:23,270 --> 00:09:24,580
Senior, senior...

136
00:09:24,650 --> 00:09:26,150
May I add you on WeChat?

137
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:31,740
Thank you, senior.

138
00:09:31,830 --> 00:09:32,820
Playboy.

139
00:09:38,910 --> 00:09:39,510
The road is so wide.

140
00:09:39,510 --> 00:09:40,510
Are you blind?

141
00:09:40,870 --> 00:09:42,330
Keep your eyes on the road,

142
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:44,120
not on pretty girls.

143
00:09:48,370 --> 00:09:50,370
What nonsense is she talking about?

144
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:51,770
How baffling.

145
00:09:59,270 --> 00:10:00,400
It's scorching hot.

146
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:01,510
I'm back.

147
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:03,960
Did you find the registration place?

148
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,050
It's right by the East Gate.

149
00:10:05,050 --> 00:10:06,010
It's crazy hot out there.

150
00:10:06,010 --> 00:10:07,810
Good thing Lili got to stay here.

151
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:11,510
Lili.

152
00:10:12,770 --> 00:10:14,620
Why is your face so red?

153
00:10:16,650 --> 00:10:17,460
Is it?

154
00:10:19,890 --> 00:10:21,300
Maybe it's t-too hot.

155
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:23,370
That's true.

156
00:10:23,870 --> 00:10:24,860
It's super hot.

157
00:10:25,250 --> 00:10:26,460
I was only out for 10 minutes,

158
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:27,720
and I almost "melted."

159
00:10:28,270 --> 00:10:29,080
Buckle up.

160
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:42,460
It's packed with people

161
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:43,860
registering at this time.

162
00:10:43,860 --> 00:10:45,530
We should have come in another time slot.

163
00:10:45,530 --> 00:10:45,960
Mm.

164
00:10:46,750 --> 00:10:48,510
And it's really hot today.

165
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:49,650
Are you feeling hot?

166
00:10:49,650 --> 00:10:50,150
Mm.

167
00:10:53,010 --> 00:10:54,540
Did Fu Shize drive you over?

168
00:10:56,130 --> 00:10:56,740
Mm.

169
00:10:59,870 --> 00:11:00,860
Why are you

170
00:11:00,860 --> 00:11:02,010
like a "mm" machine today?

171
00:11:02,010 --> 00:11:04,340
You just reply with "mm"
to whatever I say.

172
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:05,580
Maybe because someone

173
00:11:05,580 --> 00:11:07,410
kept saying "mm" to me,

174
00:11:07,550 --> 00:11:09,080
I picked up this habit, too.

175
00:11:09,620 --> 00:11:10,120
"Mm."

176
00:11:10,870 --> 00:11:12,270
You mean Fu Shize, right?

177
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:13,000
Mm.

178
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:16,770
People subconsciously

179
00:11:16,770 --> 00:11:18,250
imitate the ones they like.

180
00:11:18,250 --> 00:11:19,370
In psychology,

181
00:11:19,370 --> 00:11:21,150
this is called mirroring.

182
00:11:22,530 --> 00:11:23,510
It just kind of

183
00:11:23,510 --> 00:11:24,390
bothers me.

184
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:26,150
No matter what I say to him,

185
00:11:26,150 --> 00:11:27,460
he just responds with "mm."

186
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:28,170
Then I don't know

187
00:11:28,170 --> 00:11:30,170
how to keep the conversation going.

188
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:32,250
It's especially true for me.

189
00:11:32,770 --> 00:11:34,050
Isn't that great?

190
00:11:34,270 --> 00:11:35,360
You can ask him directly

191
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:36,890
if he can be your boyfriend.

192
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:37,890
He'll say, "Mm."

193
00:11:38,010 --> 00:11:38,960
You ask to borrow a million from him,

194
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:40,420
and he'll still say, "Mm."

195
00:11:41,820 --> 00:11:42,620
That's right.

196
00:11:42,870 --> 00:11:45,130
Crack the hard nut with another hard nut.

197
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:46,550
Let's go.

198
00:11:46,620 --> 00:11:47,120
Mm.

199
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:16,270
Hello, welcome.

200
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:18,200
Hello, welcome.

201
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:39,350
I've seen you waiting here
for a long time.

202
00:12:39,350 --> 00:12:41,350
Are you waiting for the rain to stop?

203
00:12:44,870 --> 00:12:45,870
This rain won't stop

204
00:12:45,870 --> 00:12:47,130
anytime soon, I think.

205
00:12:48,290 --> 00:12:49,420
Take this umbrella.

206
00:12:49,970 --> 00:12:51,060
But what about you?

207
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:53,090
It'll still be a while
before I get off work.

208
00:12:53,090 --> 00:12:55,220
Hopefully, the rain will stop by then.

209
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:57,350
It's fine.

210
00:12:57,350 --> 00:12:59,350
You can return it to me another time.

211
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:05,270
Thank you.

212
00:13:07,850 --> 00:13:08,690
Welcome.

213
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:42,940
Senior,

214
00:13:42,940 --> 00:13:43,740
does our advisor

215
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:45,600
not usually hold group meetings?

216
00:13:46,870 --> 00:13:47,800
Group meetings?

217
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:52,940
You want to meet Mr. Zhang?

218
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:54,910
Then you should email him early.

219
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:55,480
Otherwise,

220
00:13:55,480 --> 00:13:57,080
you'll never see him in this lifetime.

221
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:58,500
Remember to send a few more,

222
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,030
or he probably won't reply.

223
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:04,580
2D planar rotation matrix.

224
00:14:04,870 --> 00:14:06,270
What is a matrix?

225
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,220
On the surface,

226
00:14:08,270 --> 00:14:10,750
a matrix is numbers
arranged in a rectangular array...

227
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:11,550
Yun Li.

228
00:14:12,790 --> 00:14:13,420
Lili!

229
00:14:14,340 --> 00:14:15,820
But from a geometric perspective...

230
00:14:15,820 --> 00:14:16,530
Come out.

231
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:19,080
You should remember this—

232
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:21,370
a matrix is a change of coordinates.

233
00:14:22,030 --> 00:14:23,840
In a coordinate system,

234
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:25,320
all operations involve...

235
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:26,670
Why did you come in?

236
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:29,260
Be it translating a point

237
00:14:29,630 --> 00:14:31,250
or rotating an object...

238
00:14:31,250 --> 00:14:32,640
Let's have lunch together today.

239
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:33,990
Our club has recruited new members.

240
00:14:33,990 --> 00:14:34,540
The seniors

241
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:35,840
invited us to have lunch together.

242
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:37,480
You can come and get to know them.

243
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,580
I'm not going.

244
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:40,050
I can't go.

245
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:41,630
There are way too many people. I...

246
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:42,440
I'm not going.

247
00:14:43,130 --> 00:14:43,980
Go join us.

248
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:45,150
Nope.

249
00:14:48,340 --> 00:14:50,100
You look so busy.

250
00:14:51,630 --> 00:14:52,270
Yeah.

251
00:14:52,270 --> 00:14:53,010
So,

252
00:14:53,130 --> 00:14:54,980
you should go have lunch first.

253
00:14:55,220 --> 00:14:56,770
Your club won't do without you.

254
00:14:56,770 --> 00:14:58,530
Go, go ahead.

255
00:15:00,010 --> 00:15:02,240
Then remember to come
if you're free this afternoon.

256
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:04,840
I'll give it some thought.

257
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:08,140
Make sure you come.

258
00:15:08,820 --> 00:15:09,290
I'm off.

259
00:15:38,370 --> 00:15:39,170
Hello.

260
00:15:39,850 --> 00:15:40,510
Lili,

261
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:41,840
are you at school?

262
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:44,080
Fu-Fu Zhengchu?

263
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:45,840
It's the club fair today.

264
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:47,500
Come and have fun at our booth.

265
00:15:47,620 --> 00:15:48,820
Why are you using

266
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:50,440
your uncle's phone?

267
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:51,440
My phone is dead.

268
00:15:51,440 --> 00:15:52,340
My uncle came to help,

269
00:15:52,340 --> 00:15:53,390
so I used his phone.

270
00:15:53,390 --> 00:15:54,120
Come over first.

271
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,720
Let's chat when you get here.

272
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:01,290
He came to our school?

273
00:16:02,590 --> 00:16:04,320
[Club Fair]

274
00:16:14,670 --> 00:16:15,480
Hello, miss,

275
00:16:15,510 --> 00:16:16,720
check out the mountaineering club.

276
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:17,550
No, thanks.

277
00:16:17,550 --> 00:16:18,270
Please take it.

278
00:16:18,270 --> 00:16:19,340
If you change your mind,

279
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:20,240
you can join our club

280
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:21,010
anytime.

281
00:16:25,250 --> 00:16:25,980
Lili!

282
00:16:26,250 --> 00:16:26,860
Over here!

283
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:30,720
Forget about these.

284
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:32,030
Check out ours.

285
00:16:32,330 --> 00:16:33,500
Our skateboard club

286
00:16:33,530 --> 00:16:34,240
is one

287
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:36,840
of the few outdoor clubs in our school.

288
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:39,630
And check out

289
00:16:39,630 --> 00:16:40,740
all the sponsorships here.

290
00:16:40,740 --> 00:16:42,440
I, the president, got them all by myself.

291
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:43,570
Isn't that awesome?

292
00:16:46,270 --> 00:16:47,960
With this flyer,

293
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:48,740
you get a 20% discount

294
00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:50,220
at EAW.

295
00:16:50,620 --> 00:16:52,910
You're taking advantage of your relative,

296
00:16:52,910 --> 00:16:54,220
aren't you?

297
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:56,080
What do you mean by "taking advantage"?

298
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:56,720
Look carefully.

299
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:59,180
This is called a commercial collaboration.

300
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:00,980
Senior, can we sign up?

301
00:17:02,250 --> 00:17:03,280
Fill out a form first.

302
00:17:03,280 --> 00:17:03,780
Okay.

303
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:07,069
Lili,

304
00:17:07,220 --> 00:17:07,720
let me take you

305
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:08,960
to say hi to my uncle.

306
00:17:09,010 --> 00:17:09,720
Don't bother.

307
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:10,980
No need to disturb him.

308
00:17:12,980 --> 00:17:14,710
See? My uncle may be

309
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:16,440
a bit cold usually,

310
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:17,950
but he is still very popular with girls.

311
00:17:17,950 --> 00:17:18,819
This is already

312
00:17:18,849 --> 00:17:19,980
the fifth one today.

313
00:17:22,510 --> 00:17:23,310
Hey!

314
00:17:23,310 --> 00:17:24,380
Over here...

315
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:27,180
Senior,

316
00:17:27,480 --> 00:17:29,240
what is this device for?

317
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:30,200
VR experience.

318
00:17:31,030 --> 00:17:32,110
Can I try it?

319
00:17:33,510 --> 00:17:35,440
You can register over there first.

320
00:17:40,110 --> 00:17:41,200
Congratulations to Unique

321
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,830
on winning the national championship!

322
00:17:42,830 --> 00:17:44,220
I'd like to interview the captain,

323
00:17:44,220 --> 00:17:44,940
Fu Shize.

324
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:47,030
The national championship trophy

325
00:17:47,030 --> 00:17:48,270
is once again engraved

326
00:17:48,270 --> 00:17:48,960
with Unique's

327
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:49,830
crescent-shaped emblem.

328
00:17:49,830 --> 00:17:50,920
I heard you designed

329
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:52,070
this team emblem yourself.

330
00:17:52,070 --> 00:17:53,930
Does it have any special meaning?

331
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:57,080
The crescent represents renewal and hope,

332
00:17:57,370 --> 00:17:59,520
guiding us to break through the darkness

333
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:01,650
and bravely venture into the unknown.

334
00:18:07,590 --> 00:18:08,180
Lili.

335
00:18:08,950 --> 00:18:10,000
Is there anything you like?

336
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,330
Pick whatever you like.

337
00:18:16,010 --> 00:18:16,810
Lili!

338
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:17,940
What's wrong?

339
00:18:20,010 --> 00:18:20,740
Why isn't this

340
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:22,110
the logo

341
00:18:22,110 --> 00:18:22,770
of EAW?

342
00:18:23,980 --> 00:18:24,980
Oh, you mean this.

343
00:18:25,370 --> 00:18:26,850
My uncle had a team

344
00:18:26,870 --> 00:18:27,730
back in college.

345
00:18:27,730 --> 00:18:29,330
It's their old merchandise,

346
00:18:29,530 --> 00:18:30,330
kept at home

347
00:18:30,330 --> 00:18:30,980
for a long time.

348
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:32,980
So I brought it here to use as a prize.

349
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:35,460
Pick a power bank.

350
00:18:35,460 --> 00:18:37,030
It's our most expensive item today.

351
00:18:37,030 --> 00:18:38,160
Is that really okay?

352
00:18:38,330 --> 00:18:39,640
Don't be shy.

353
00:18:40,330 --> 00:18:40,610
They're

354
00:18:40,610 --> 00:18:41,810
all sponsored by EAW.

355
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:46,820
Here you are, the flyers.

356
00:18:50,550 --> 00:18:52,280
Do I have to hand out all of them?

357
00:18:52,780 --> 00:18:54,140
Isn't it stated in the contract?

358
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:56,140
There are still too many of them.

359
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:57,500
EAW only sponsored

360
00:18:57,500 --> 00:18:58,240
this little.

361
00:18:58,270 --> 00:18:59,230
I don't think this will do.

362
00:18:59,230 --> 00:18:59,790
Uncle,

363
00:18:59,810 --> 00:19:00,870
don't you think so?

364
00:19:01,380 --> 00:19:02,040
No, I don't.

365
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:03,400
Why?

366
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:06,380
I'm not the one to hand them out.

367
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:06,900
You...

368
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:09,920
I can help hand them out.

369
00:19:15,850 --> 00:19:16,610
Uncle,

370
00:19:16,610 --> 00:19:17,310
look,

371
00:19:17,310 --> 00:19:17,980
this is

372
00:19:17,980 --> 00:19:20,040
the difference between you and Lili.

373
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:30,720
Uncle,

374
00:19:30,980 --> 00:19:32,850
why are you not helping me hand them out?

375
00:19:32,850 --> 00:19:35,050
This is the difference between you two.

376
00:20:05,090 --> 00:20:06,000
Fu Shize?

377
00:20:07,770 --> 00:20:09,770
I didn't expect to run into you here.

378
00:20:12,770 --> 00:20:14,170
What brings you to Nanwu?

379
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:16,480
My cousin got admitted to NUST.

380
00:20:16,530 --> 00:20:17,640
I brought him out to walk around

381
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:18,570
and relax a bit.

382
00:20:21,250 --> 00:20:22,510
Come on, take a look...

383
00:20:23,090 --> 00:20:24,660
Who is this girl?

384
00:20:25,050 --> 00:20:27,810
She seems to be Fu Shize's acquaintance.

385
00:20:27,810 --> 00:20:28,590
How are you

386
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:30,440
doing lately?

387
00:20:31,850 --> 00:20:32,650
I'm good.

388
00:20:33,610 --> 00:20:34,470
What about you?

389
00:20:39,750 --> 00:20:40,750
Glad to know that.

390
00:20:48,570 --> 00:20:49,740
Fu Zhengchu.

391
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:52,770
What's wrong, Lili?

392
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:54,790
Is that your uncle's

393
00:20:54,790 --> 00:20:55,660
girlfriend?

394
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:00,290
He's never dated anyone.

395
00:21:00,290 --> 00:21:02,020
How could he have a girlfriend?

396
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:03,960
Lili,

397
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:04,550
you hand them out here,

398
00:21:04,550 --> 00:21:05,810
and I'll go over there.

399
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:22,270
Then should I

400
00:21:22,310 --> 00:21:24,710
take the initiative
to make the first move?

401
00:22:08,940 --> 00:22:09,850
I won a prize!

402
00:22:10,510 --> 00:22:11,040
This way.

403
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:16,500
I want this canvas bag.

404
00:22:22,440 --> 00:22:23,460
Have some water.

405
00:22:39,740 --> 00:22:41,540
I wasn't asking you to help me...

406
00:22:45,980 --> 00:22:46,660
Thank you.

407
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:56,640
Make your choice.

408
00:22:57,160 --> 00:22:58,350
We have power banks,

409
00:22:58,350 --> 00:22:58,940
bottles,

410
00:22:58,940 --> 00:22:59,870
and canvas bags.

411
00:23:01,830 --> 00:23:02,890
I want a canvas bag.

412
00:23:03,980 --> 00:23:05,110
This is the last one.

413
00:23:05,110 --> 00:23:06,170
Congratulations.

414
00:23:06,510 --> 00:23:07,310
Thank you.

415
00:23:11,100 --> 00:23:13,100
The skateboard club is recruiting!

416
00:23:14,220 --> 00:23:14,950
Here you are.

417
00:23:21,290 --> 00:23:22,690
Isn't this what you want?

418
00:23:30,510 --> 00:23:31,310
Thank you.

419
00:23:47,070 --> 00:23:48,380
Don't you feel bad

420
00:23:48,380 --> 00:23:50,580
letting your uncle line up there alone?

421
00:23:50,660 --> 00:23:52,310
How about we go line up with him?

422
00:23:52,310 --> 00:23:53,050
It's fine.

423
00:23:53,050 --> 00:23:54,680
My uncle is experienced in lining up.

424
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:56,310
Whenever we hung out before,

425
00:23:56,380 --> 00:23:57,380
my uncle was the one

426
00:23:57,380 --> 00:23:58,980
who queued up and paid the bills.

427
00:23:58,980 --> 00:24:00,110
Lili, you know what?

428
00:24:00,250 --> 00:24:00,880
When we were little,

429
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:01,960
as long as my sister and I

430
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:03,010
called him Uncle,

431
00:24:03,180 --> 00:24:04,940
we basically got whatever we wanted.

432
00:24:04,940 --> 00:24:06,180
He treats us younger generation

433
00:24:06,180 --> 00:24:06,910
really well.

434
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:08,480
Lili.

435
00:24:09,570 --> 00:24:11,050
Are you from Xifu?

436
00:24:12,180 --> 00:24:12,810
Yes.

437
00:24:12,810 --> 00:24:14,070
I lived in Xifu

438
00:24:14,070 --> 00:24:15,610
until I started my master's.

439
00:24:15,610 --> 00:24:17,550
Then you must be a straight-A student
at XUST.

440
00:24:17,550 --> 00:24:18,350
Nope.

441
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:19,720
I'm just an undergraduate

442
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:21,750
from a regular first-tier university
in Xifu.

443
00:24:21,750 --> 00:24:23,610
Then why didn't you apply to XUST?

444
00:24:24,510 --> 00:24:26,310
I wanted to,

445
00:24:26,310 --> 00:24:27,370
but I didn't get in.

446
00:24:27,550 --> 00:24:29,550
Not everyone can get admitted to it.

447
00:24:29,660 --> 00:24:30,460
That's true.

448
00:24:30,480 --> 00:24:32,210
My uncle is no ordinary person.

449
00:24:39,850 --> 00:24:42,010
You're from XUST?

450
00:24:44,220 --> 00:24:45,050
Lili,

451
00:24:45,220 --> 00:24:46,350
you don't know that?

452
00:24:46,460 --> 00:24:48,350
My uncle is not only from XUST

453
00:24:48,350 --> 00:24:49,920
but also the youngest top scorer

454
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:51,750
in the college entrance exam
in the history of Nanwu.

455
00:24:51,750 --> 00:24:52,350
He was a few years

456
00:24:52,350 --> 00:24:54,010
younger than his classmates.

457
00:24:57,850 --> 00:24:58,660
Uncle,

458
00:24:58,660 --> 00:24:59,790
where are you going?

459
00:25:00,660 --> 00:25:01,680
He's getting shy.

460
00:25:04,070 --> 00:25:04,810
Lili,

461
00:25:04,960 --> 00:25:05,680
you have no idea

462
00:25:05,680 --> 00:25:07,410
how hateful my uncle used to be.

463
00:25:07,960 --> 00:25:08,660
When I was little,

464
00:25:08,660 --> 00:25:10,480
I was too scared to go to school.

465
00:25:10,610 --> 00:25:11,740
My uncle told me that

466
00:25:12,250 --> 00:25:13,680
since we were in the same school,

467
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:15,270
he would go to school with me every day

468
00:25:15,270 --> 00:25:16,270
and protect me.

469
00:25:16,310 --> 00:25:17,110
And I believed

470
00:25:17,110 --> 00:25:17,960
what he said.

471
00:25:18,310 --> 00:25:19,110
But in the end,

472
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:21,570
he only accompanied me for 2 months,

473
00:25:21,570 --> 00:25:22,160
and then he...

474
00:25:22,160 --> 00:25:23,220
He skipped a grade.

475
00:25:23,460 --> 00:25:24,250
Yes.

476
00:25:25,960 --> 00:25:26,770
Lili.

477
00:25:28,250 --> 00:25:29,250
How do you know?

478
00:25:30,510 --> 00:25:31,920
Didn't you just say that

479
00:25:31,920 --> 00:25:33,920
he was younger than his classmates?

480
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:35,960
My uncle did his bachelor's,

481
00:25:35,960 --> 00:25:37,610
master's, and PhD all at XUST.

482
00:25:37,610 --> 00:25:39,160
If he hadn't taken a leave of absence,

483
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:40,900
he would have finished his PhD by now.

484
00:25:40,900 --> 00:25:41,960
A leave of absence?

485
00:25:43,180 --> 00:25:43,770
A gap year—

486
00:25:43,770 --> 00:25:45,510
isn't it popular now?

487
00:25:46,250 --> 00:25:47,580
Anyway, he's in no rush.

488
00:25:47,850 --> 00:25:49,920
He started school earlier than others.

489
00:25:49,920 --> 00:25:51,480
If he goes back now,

490
00:25:51,510 --> 00:25:52,420
he might even run

491
00:25:52,420 --> 00:25:53,820
into his old classmates.

492
00:25:58,380 --> 00:25:59,180
Fu Zhengchu,

493
00:25:59,570 --> 00:26:00,270
I have a question.

494
00:26:00,270 --> 00:26:02,420
Did you and your uncle

495
00:26:02,420 --> 00:26:04,050
use to chat

496
00:26:04,050 --> 00:26:05,510
the way we do?

497
00:26:05,920 --> 00:26:06,850
Yes, of course.

498
00:26:06,880 --> 00:26:07,810
But my uncle

499
00:26:07,810 --> 00:26:08,750
used to be more talkative.

500
00:26:08,750 --> 00:26:09,550
Now...

501
00:26:10,380 --> 00:26:11,440
he's changed a bit.

502
00:26:15,070 --> 00:26:15,610
Uncle,

503
00:26:16,010 --> 00:26:16,740
you're back.

504
00:26:30,010 --> 00:26:30,740
Thank you.

505
00:27:08,180 --> 00:27:09,420
My uncle did his bachelor's,

506
00:27:09,420 --> 00:27:11,080
master's, and PhD all at XUST.

507
00:27:11,350 --> 00:27:12,810
If he hadn't taken a leave of absence,

508
00:27:12,810 --> 00:27:14,870
he would have finished his PhD by now.

509
00:27:46,810 --> 00:27:48,270
What exactly happened

510
00:27:48,530 --> 00:27:50,530
during his 2-year leave of absence?

511
00:27:51,050 --> 00:27:51,810
Why did he

512
00:27:51,810 --> 00:27:53,110
change so greatly?

513
00:28:13,480 --> 00:28:14,010
Lili.

514
00:28:16,770 --> 00:28:19,770
Why are you studying at the library
even on a Saturday?

515
00:28:20,110 --> 00:28:22,170
There are fewer people on Saturdays.

516
00:28:24,180 --> 00:28:24,760
Look,

517
00:28:24,850 --> 00:28:26,570
the weather is so nice out there.

518
00:28:26,570 --> 00:28:29,070
It's a waste of youth to stay here.

519
00:28:30,610 --> 00:28:31,740
Then let me waste it.

520
00:28:32,640 --> 00:28:33,180
Let's go.

521
00:28:34,940 --> 00:28:35,680
Let's go.

522
00:28:38,590 --> 00:28:39,050
Come on.

523
00:28:48,310 --> 00:28:49,980
Look at your little face

524
00:28:49,980 --> 00:28:51,370
and your complexion.

525
00:28:51,510 --> 00:28:52,660
You should hang out more

526
00:28:52,660 --> 00:28:54,850
to bask in the sun.

527
00:28:56,720 --> 00:28:57,720
Forget about it.

528
00:28:58,680 --> 00:29:00,620
I still have to stay strong
and work independently.

529
00:29:00,620 --> 00:29:01,740
Otherwise, my 3 years of graduate school

530
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:03,570
will end up like medical school.

531
00:29:04,220 --> 00:29:05,180
You know what?

532
00:29:05,510 --> 00:29:06,760
I finally met

533
00:29:06,780 --> 00:29:08,710
my graduate advisor the other day.

534
00:29:09,570 --> 00:29:10,420
Then I asked him,

535
00:29:10,420 --> 00:29:11,380
"Do you have any advice

536
00:29:11,380 --> 00:29:12,640
on my research focus?"

537
00:29:12,850 --> 00:29:13,810
And he said...

538
00:29:14,610 --> 00:29:16,610
Your proposal is quite impressive.

539
00:29:17,610 --> 00:29:19,050
I happen to have a college classmate

540
00:29:19,050 --> 00:29:20,350
who is a professor overseas.

541
00:29:20,350 --> 00:29:21,610
If you're interested,

542
00:29:21,660 --> 00:29:22,420
I can recommend you

543
00:29:22,420 --> 00:29:24,480
for his lab to study there for a while.

544
00:29:24,570 --> 00:29:26,980
Then what about my thesis?

545
00:29:27,310 --> 00:29:28,770
You can write your thesis abroad,

546
00:29:28,770 --> 00:29:29,610
then translate it into Chinese,

547
00:29:29,610 --> 00:29:30,790
and mail it back.

548
00:29:32,050 --> 00:29:33,070
I thought,

549
00:29:33,070 --> 00:29:35,160
such a nice exchange student opportunity
that fell on me

550
00:29:35,160 --> 00:29:36,050
must be

551
00:29:36,070 --> 00:29:37,220
a short-term one,

552
00:29:37,250 --> 00:29:39,110
lasting about half a year or so.

553
00:29:39,250 --> 00:29:40,420
But guess what he said?

554
00:29:40,420 --> 00:29:41,280
What did he say?

555
00:29:42,380 --> 00:29:44,010
"Why don't you stay for 3 full years

556
00:29:44,010 --> 00:29:45,210
before coming back?"

557
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:48,350
What kind of advisor is that?

558
00:29:48,350 --> 00:29:49,840
I can't believe it.

559
00:29:51,900 --> 00:29:52,850
Guess

560
00:29:53,160 --> 00:29:55,820
I have to find my own way out
over the next 3 years.

561
00:30:04,250 --> 00:30:04,920
Yun Ye?

562
00:30:06,140 --> 00:30:06,810
Hello?

563
00:30:07,460 --> 00:30:08,250
Hello, Li.

564
00:30:08,480 --> 00:30:09,770
Emergency.

565
00:30:09,880 --> 00:30:10,950
Can you lend me some money?

566
00:30:10,950 --> 00:30:12,480
You're asking me for money?

567
00:30:12,790 --> 00:30:13,670
Did you forget that my money

568
00:30:13,670 --> 00:30:15,000
was all withheld by Dad?

569
00:30:15,160 --> 00:30:16,180
I even have

570
00:30:16,180 --> 00:30:18,180
to find an internship to make money now.

571
00:30:18,180 --> 00:30:19,510
I don't care about that.

572
00:30:19,880 --> 00:30:21,220
Dad cut my allowance

573
00:30:21,220 --> 00:30:21,850
in half

574
00:30:21,850 --> 00:30:23,310
because I spoke up for you.

575
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:24,070
You know what?

576
00:30:24,070 --> 00:30:24,870
A few days ago,

577
00:30:24,920 --> 00:30:25,940
he was going to rush to Nanwu

578
00:30:25,940 --> 00:30:26,880
and get you back.

579
00:30:27,260 --> 00:30:29,180
Fortunately, I stepped in quickly

580
00:30:29,180 --> 00:30:30,250
and stopped him.

581
00:30:30,770 --> 00:30:31,900
Now I'm out of money.

582
00:30:32,070 --> 00:30:32,750
Shouldn't you

583
00:30:32,750 --> 00:30:33,880
compensate me a bit?

584
00:30:34,110 --> 00:30:35,920
Your dad is way too ruthless.

585
00:30:36,370 --> 00:30:38,590
Anyway,
just transfer 200 yuan to me first.

586
00:30:38,590 --> 00:30:39,480
When I

587
00:30:39,480 --> 00:30:40,550
get paid from my part-time job,

588
00:30:40,550 --> 00:30:41,510
I'll pay you back.

589
00:30:41,510 --> 00:30:42,180
Hold on.

590
00:30:42,590 --> 00:30:44,250
You're doing a part-time job?

591
00:30:44,350 --> 00:30:45,510
As a high school sophomore, how can you

592
00:30:45,510 --> 00:30:46,460
work part-time instead of studying?

593
00:30:46,460 --> 00:30:47,740
What about your college entrance exam?

594
00:30:47,740 --> 00:30:49,270
Uncle's convenience store
is short-staffed.

595
00:30:49,270 --> 00:30:50,510
I just come and help out occasionally

596
00:30:50,510 --> 00:30:51,970
to earn some pocket money.

597
00:30:52,160 --> 00:30:53,240
Don't worry too much.

598
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:54,970
Just transfer the money first.

599
00:30:57,290 --> 00:30:57,940
Fine,

600
00:30:57,940 --> 00:30:58,880
I'll transfer 200 yuan to you,

601
00:30:58,880 --> 00:31:00,480
but stop working part-time.

602
00:31:00,560 --> 00:31:01,690
I'll think about it.

603
00:31:01,960 --> 00:31:02,550
Yun Ye...

604
00:31:04,880 --> 00:31:06,120
He's doing a part-time job.

605
00:31:06,120 --> 00:31:06,960
Didn't your dad

606
00:31:06,960 --> 00:31:08,340
push Yun Ye into this?

607
00:31:08,980 --> 00:31:10,240
You two siblings are

608
00:31:10,330 --> 00:31:12,610
really like a beggar and a panhandler.

609
00:31:14,570 --> 00:31:15,310
Where do you plan

610
00:31:15,310 --> 00:31:16,720
to get your part-time job next?

611
00:31:16,720 --> 00:31:17,950
I'm going to EAW.

612
00:31:18,490 --> 00:31:19,990
That's right!

613
00:31:22,610 --> 00:31:24,220
Working in EAW

614
00:31:24,220 --> 00:31:25,380
will give you an advantage

615
00:31:25,380 --> 00:31:26,440
in getting your "moon"

616
00:31:26,440 --> 00:31:27,270
very soon.

617
00:31:27,440 --> 00:31:30,110
A harvest in both career and love.

618
00:31:30,810 --> 00:31:32,240
I haven't even gotten closer to him yet.

619
00:31:32,240 --> 00:31:33,420
What's there to get?

620
00:31:33,420 --> 00:31:34,310
You can do it!

621
00:31:34,330 --> 00:31:35,660
Stop talking nonsense.

622
00:31:40,320 --> 00:31:41,920
Speaking of career, here comes a call.

623
00:31:41,920 --> 00:31:42,980
Answer it quickly.

624
00:31:44,610 --> 00:31:45,810
Hello, Jiameng.

625
00:31:46,140 --> 00:31:46,920
Yun Li,

626
00:31:46,920 --> 00:31:48,240
we received your resume.

627
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:50,220
Are you available for an interview?

628
00:31:50,220 --> 00:31:51,350
Yes, I'm available.

629
00:31:51,420 --> 00:31:51,980
Okay,

630
00:31:51,980 --> 00:31:52,610
we will send you

631
00:31:52,610 --> 00:31:53,810
a text notification shortly.

632
00:31:53,810 --> 00:31:54,830
See you then.

633
00:31:55,180 --> 00:31:55,700
Okay.

634
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:02,230
[Yun Li] [Skills & Expertise]

635
00:32:07,590 --> 00:32:09,160
Yun Li, right?

636
00:32:12,030 --> 00:32:12,960
You've been

637
00:32:12,960 --> 00:32:14,200
well-prepared.

638
00:32:14,700 --> 00:32:16,140
But your profile indicates that you're

639
00:32:16,140 --> 00:32:18,270
just in your first year of grad school.

640
00:32:19,330 --> 00:32:20,050
What made you decide

641
00:32:20,050 --> 00:32:21,850
to apply for an internship here?

642
00:32:23,250 --> 00:32:24,090
Because...

643
00:32:24,830 --> 00:32:26,290
Because the automation major

644
00:32:26,290 --> 00:32:28,090
requires not only theoretical knowledge

645
00:32:28,090 --> 00:32:29,940
but also practical experience.

646
00:32:30,330 --> 00:32:32,350
So I'd like to intern early

647
00:32:32,500 --> 00:32:34,100
and apply what I've learned.

648
00:32:34,250 --> 00:32:35,350
Yun Li, right?

649
00:32:39,030 --> 00:32:40,250
Have you had

650
00:32:40,440 --> 00:32:42,460
any relevant internships before?

651
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:49,330
No.

652
00:32:51,850 --> 00:32:52,750
Our engineering department

653
00:32:52,750 --> 00:32:55,160
is full of graduates
from top universities.

654
00:32:55,160 --> 00:32:58,460
Your undergraduate school is just average.

655
00:32:59,740 --> 00:33:01,470
Do you have any special skills?

656
00:33:03,290 --> 00:33:05,550
My undergraduate degree may be average,

657
00:33:05,620 --> 00:33:06,350
but if

658
00:33:06,350 --> 00:33:07,950
you could give me a chance...

659
00:33:08,850 --> 00:33:10,160
This is not a school.

660
00:33:11,290 --> 00:33:12,050
Also,

661
00:33:12,050 --> 00:33:13,550
I've been talking to you,

662
00:33:14,330 --> 00:33:15,960
and you haven't stopped fidgeting.

663
00:33:15,960 --> 00:33:18,420
Don't you think
you're a bit disrespectful?

664
00:33:19,530 --> 00:33:20,400
Sir,

665
00:33:20,960 --> 00:33:21,890
you got me wrong.

666
00:33:21,900 --> 00:33:23,700
I didn't mean to disrespect you.

667
00:33:23,750 --> 00:33:25,090
Please let me finish.

668
00:33:29,940 --> 00:33:31,340
Besides being a student,

669
00:33:31,350 --> 00:33:32,500
I am also a tech DIY content creator

670
00:33:32,500 --> 00:33:33,460
on EAW.

671
00:33:34,160 --> 00:33:35,530
I have done many reviews and tests

672
00:33:35,530 --> 00:33:36,750
on digital products.

673
00:33:37,330 --> 00:33:38,960
So I can not only understand
developers' thinking

674
00:33:38,960 --> 00:33:40,820
from a professional perspective

675
00:33:40,900 --> 00:33:42,550
but also provide objective takes

676
00:33:42,550 --> 00:33:43,960
from the average user's point of view.

677
00:33:43,960 --> 00:33:45,460
I think this is my value.

678
00:33:47,050 --> 00:33:48,030
Your value

679
00:33:48,900 --> 00:33:50,400
sounds too illusory.

680
00:33:51,700 --> 00:33:52,310
Alright,

681
00:33:52,500 --> 00:33:53,050
Yun Li,

682
00:33:53,350 --> 00:33:54,960
that's all for today's interview.

683
00:33:54,960 --> 00:33:57,360
We will notify you
if there are any updates.

684
00:34:18,190 --> 00:34:19,960
I guess I failed the interview.

685
00:34:21,090 --> 00:34:21,900
Handsome,

686
00:34:22,300 --> 00:34:23,610
may I add you on WeChat?

687
00:34:24,150 --> 00:34:24,800
Nope.

688
00:34:26,330 --> 00:34:27,500
Ms. Idle Crowd?

689
00:34:30,460 --> 00:34:31,420
Ms. Idle Crowd!

690
00:34:34,090 --> 00:34:35,889
I'm calling you. Come over here.

691
00:34:41,730 --> 00:34:42,510
Come on.

692
00:34:45,170 --> 00:34:46,360
Ms. Idle Crowd,

693
00:34:46,980 --> 00:34:48,980
didn't you just ask me to help you

694
00:34:48,980 --> 00:34:50,780
get this handsome guy's WeChat?

695
00:34:51,210 --> 00:34:53,170
He thought I wanted it.

696
00:34:53,570 --> 00:34:55,170
It made me so embarrassed.

697
00:34:55,960 --> 00:34:56,620
You want it?

698
00:34:58,320 --> 00:34:58,880
Yeah.

699
00:34:59,940 --> 00:35:01,320
She was just too shy

700
00:35:01,320 --> 00:35:02,450
to tell you herself.

701
00:35:03,920 --> 00:35:05,650
Didn't I already give it to you?

702
00:35:08,570 --> 00:35:10,100
So you already asked for it?

703
00:35:13,570 --> 00:35:15,010
This is a mess.

704
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:17,520
If you need anything,

705
00:35:18,110 --> 00:35:19,910
you can just come to me directly.

706
00:35:23,570 --> 00:35:24,630
I'll take my leave.

707
00:35:30,170 --> 00:35:32,100
So you two already knew each other.

708
00:35:35,550 --> 00:35:36,380
Kind of.

709
00:35:37,380 --> 00:35:39,440
Then you should have told me earlier.

710
00:35:39,860 --> 00:35:40,760
And I definitely wouldn't

711
00:35:40,760 --> 00:35:42,070
have done such a thing.

712
00:35:42,510 --> 00:35:44,440
It made me quite embarrassed, too.

713
00:35:46,170 --> 00:35:46,820
Forget it.

714
00:35:48,550 --> 00:35:49,360
However,

715
00:35:50,280 --> 00:35:52,010
when did you ask for his WeChat?

716
00:35:52,320 --> 00:35:53,110
Ms. Idle Crowd,

717
00:35:53,110 --> 00:35:54,210
I didn't know

718
00:35:55,180 --> 00:35:56,110
you had it in you.

719
00:35:56,570 --> 00:35:58,010
It's not what you think.

720
00:35:59,110 --> 00:36:00,070
No worries,

721
00:36:00,210 --> 00:36:01,570
I'm not going to fight you for him.

722
00:36:01,570 --> 00:36:02,820
This kind of poor...

723
00:36:04,030 --> 00:36:06,830
This kind
of incompetent maintenance technician

724
00:36:06,840 --> 00:36:08,100
is not appealing to me.

725
00:36:08,580 --> 00:36:09,980
What are you talking about?

726
00:36:09,980 --> 00:36:10,940
Didn't you see

727
00:36:11,170 --> 00:36:12,700
the dust all over his hands?

728
00:36:13,710 --> 00:36:14,940
I once thought,

729
00:36:15,320 --> 00:36:16,710
as Mr. Xu's friend,

730
00:36:16,710 --> 00:36:18,840
he would at least be part of management.

731
00:36:18,840 --> 00:36:20,100
But judging from this,

732
00:36:20,530 --> 00:36:22,730
they don't seem to be on very good terms.

733
00:36:23,840 --> 00:36:25,300
You're quite a catch, huh?

734
00:36:26,030 --> 00:36:27,040
I...

735
00:36:28,730 --> 00:36:29,670
I guess I'm not bad.

736
00:36:29,670 --> 00:36:30,640
You're such a catch,

737
00:36:30,640 --> 00:36:32,470
but he still didn't give you his WeChat.

738
00:36:32,470 --> 00:36:33,630
That's because...

739
00:36:33,630 --> 00:36:34,170
Seems like he

740
00:36:34,170 --> 00:36:35,480
has no interest in you.

741
00:36:36,510 --> 00:36:37,780
So how outstanding he is,

742
00:36:37,780 --> 00:36:38,530
what kind of person he is,

743
00:36:38,530 --> 00:36:39,130
and how much he earns

744
00:36:39,130 --> 00:36:40,780
have nothing to do with you.

745
00:36:43,630 --> 00:36:45,780
Also, I'm Idle Cloud Tick-Tock,

746
00:36:46,030 --> 00:36:47,010
not Idle Crowd.

747
00:36:51,780 --> 00:36:53,070
She's quite fierce.

748
00:37:22,900 --> 00:37:23,630
Hello, Mom.

749
00:37:24,360 --> 00:37:25,150
Lili.

750
00:37:25,710 --> 00:37:26,640
Are you busy now?

751
00:37:27,380 --> 00:37:29,310
How are you settling in over there?

752
00:37:29,420 --> 00:37:30,760
Living there alone,

753
00:37:30,860 --> 00:37:32,380
you must take good care of yourself.

754
00:37:32,380 --> 00:37:33,840
I'm doing quite well, Mom.

755
00:37:33,980 --> 00:37:35,240
Nothing bad happened.

756
00:37:35,300 --> 00:37:35,960
Okay.

757
00:37:36,510 --> 00:37:37,510
I heard from your brother that

758
00:37:37,510 --> 00:37:38,920
you're looking for an internship.

759
00:37:38,920 --> 00:37:39,670
How is it going?

760
00:37:39,670 --> 00:37:40,870
Is it going smoothly?

761
00:37:41,050 --> 00:37:42,710
I just finished an interview.

762
00:37:42,710 --> 00:37:43,710
I don't know if they

763
00:37:43,710 --> 00:37:44,820
want me or not yet.

764
00:37:45,710 --> 00:37:47,480
It doesn't matter if they want you or not.

765
00:37:47,480 --> 00:37:48,480
Right now, for you,

766
00:37:48,480 --> 00:37:50,480
what matters most is to gain experience.

767
00:37:50,480 --> 00:37:52,150
If you feel unhappy out there,

768
00:37:52,150 --> 00:37:53,280
just come back home.

769
00:37:53,380 --> 00:37:55,040
Don't push yourself too much.

770
00:37:55,150 --> 00:37:55,960
I got it.

771
00:37:56,780 --> 00:37:58,320
She's already so introverted.

772
00:37:58,320 --> 00:37:58,980
She barely talks

773
00:37:58,980 --> 00:38:00,030
when she's out.

774
00:38:00,190 --> 00:38:01,500
With her ear like that,

775
00:38:01,500 --> 00:38:03,100
she should just stay at home.

776
00:38:03,190 --> 00:38:05,110
It's best for her to stay by our side!

777
00:38:05,110 --> 00:38:06,500
Being alone out there,

778
00:38:06,500 --> 00:38:07,320
if she gets bullied,

779
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:08,960
no one will even have her back!

780
00:38:08,960 --> 00:38:09,500
Dad.

781
00:38:10,840 --> 00:38:11,980
Do you know why

782
00:38:12,010 --> 00:38:13,940
I don't like wearing a hearing aid?

783
00:38:14,860 --> 00:38:16,460
Because I want to be a normal person.

784
00:38:16,460 --> 00:38:17,920
And I am a normal person.

785
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:18,920
I just can't hear

786
00:38:18,920 --> 00:38:20,180
in one ear. That's all.

787
00:38:20,650 --> 00:38:21,550
No one will bully me

788
00:38:21,550 --> 00:38:22,590
or look down on me

789
00:38:22,590 --> 00:38:23,440
just because

790
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:24,710
I'm deaf in one ear!

791
00:38:25,650 --> 00:38:26,960
And I've never seen it

792
00:38:27,190 --> 00:38:28,400
as a problem myself all these years.

793
00:38:28,400 --> 00:38:28,960
I don't feel like

794
00:38:28,960 --> 00:38:29,800
it has ever affected my life

795
00:38:29,800 --> 00:38:30,960
or become a burden to me.

796
00:38:30,960 --> 00:38:31,510
Why do you

797
00:38:31,510 --> 00:38:32,960
keep reminding me over and over again?

798
00:38:32,960 --> 00:38:33,690
Even if someone

799
00:38:33,690 --> 00:38:34,650
bullies me now,

800
00:38:34,650 --> 00:38:35,610
I'm capable

801
00:38:35,610 --> 00:38:36,360
of fighting back

802
00:38:36,360 --> 00:38:37,300
and protecting myself.

803
00:38:37,300 --> 00:38:38,800
I can just do fine on my own.

804
00:38:39,350 --> 00:38:40,660
Wait, what do you mean?

805
00:38:41,500 --> 00:38:42,190
Hey,

806
00:38:42,190 --> 00:38:44,120
is it wrong for me to care about you?

807
00:38:44,620 --> 00:38:45,950
How could you

808
00:38:45,980 --> 00:38:47,550
have grown up safely without me?

809
00:38:47,550 --> 00:38:48,840
And now you're telling me

810
00:38:48,840 --> 00:38:50,590
you can do fine on your own?

811
00:38:51,630 --> 00:38:52,960
I didn't put it that way.

812
00:38:53,050 --> 00:38:53,590
You didn't,

813
00:38:53,590 --> 00:38:55,120
but you thought it that way!

814
00:38:55,600 --> 00:38:57,070
Buy a plane ticket and come back.

815
00:38:57,070 --> 00:38:58,130
I'm not going back.

816
00:38:58,320 --> 00:39:00,720
Mom, if there's nothing else,
I'll hang up.

817
00:39:00,780 --> 00:39:01,440
Lili.

818
00:39:02,400 --> 00:39:03,370
You... You know

819
00:39:03,400 --> 00:39:04,860
your dad didn't mean that.

820
00:39:05,170 --> 00:39:06,120
That's enough.

821
00:39:06,140 --> 00:39:07,420
Just don't come back if you don't want to.

822
00:39:07,420 --> 00:39:08,820
Fine, I won't go back!

823
00:39:08,920 --> 00:39:09,550
My car has arrived.

824
00:39:09,550 --> 00:39:10,420
I'm hanging up.

825
00:39:27,800 --> 00:39:29,910
[Steal A Moment To Sip Wine Guesthouse]

826
00:39:38,880 --> 00:39:40,050
Lili, you're back.

827
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:42,420
Why are you soaking wet?

828
00:39:42,420 --> 00:39:43,480
Dry yourself quickly.

829
00:39:43,480 --> 00:39:44,150
Thank you.

830
00:39:45,540 --> 00:39:46,460
Just call me if you forget

831
00:39:46,460 --> 00:39:47,320
your umbrella next time,

832
00:39:47,320 --> 00:39:48,480
and I'll pick you up.

833
00:39:49,010 --> 00:39:50,410
That's too much trouble.

834
00:39:50,530 --> 00:39:51,760
What trouble?

835
00:39:51,780 --> 00:39:52,890
We are friends.

836
00:39:53,260 --> 00:39:54,960
Don't say things like that anymore.

837
00:39:54,960 --> 00:39:56,480
Have some warm water quickly.

838
00:39:56,480 --> 00:39:57,280
Thank you.

839
00:39:58,610 --> 00:39:59,420
Didn't you

840
00:39:59,420 --> 00:40:00,590
go to EAW

841
00:40:00,590 --> 00:40:01,460
for an interview today?

842
00:40:01,460 --> 00:40:03,260
How did it go? Did you get the job?

843
00:40:04,760 --> 00:40:05,820
I don't know yet.

844
00:40:06,650 --> 00:40:08,380
What do you mean you don't know?

845
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:09,760
I'll call and ask for you.

846
00:40:09,760 --> 00:40:10,500
No, don't bother.

847
00:40:10,500 --> 00:40:12,130
I'll just wait for the notice.

848
00:40:12,130 --> 00:40:13,530
I'm going back to my room.

849
00:40:28,150 --> 00:40:28,960
Yun Li,

850
00:40:30,010 --> 00:40:31,690
you can't even

851
00:40:31,690 --> 00:40:32,980
get into EAW,

852
00:40:33,830 --> 00:40:36,000
and you still want to get closer to him?

853
00:40:45,960 --> 00:40:46,460
Hello?

854
00:40:47,340 --> 00:40:49,470
This is Fang Yuning from EAW speaking.

855
00:40:49,650 --> 00:40:50,760
Hello, Ms. Fang.

856
00:40:50,760 --> 00:40:52,800
For the job you interviewed for,

857
00:40:52,800 --> 00:40:53,590
we've already found

858
00:40:53,590 --> 00:40:54,850
a suitable candidate.

859
00:40:57,050 --> 00:40:58,000
I-I see.

860
00:40:58,000 --> 00:40:58,800
Thank you.

861
00:40:59,380 --> 00:41:00,170
However,

862
00:41:00,230 --> 00:41:02,460
the publicity department
is still short-staffed.

863
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:04,120
Would you like to give it a try?

864
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:06,530
The publicity department?

865
00:41:06,960 --> 00:41:08,370
I watched the store-review videos

866
00:41:08,370 --> 00:41:09,690
you posted on EAW.

867
00:41:09,920 --> 00:41:10,920
They are well shot

868
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:12,260
with many details.

869
00:41:12,420 --> 00:41:14,480
I think you are quite suitable for it.

870
00:41:14,550 --> 00:41:16,000
Although it's not the job

871
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:17,800
you initially interviewed for,

872
00:41:18,210 --> 00:41:19,280
would you consider it?

873
00:41:19,280 --> 00:41:20,920
I don't need any more consideration.

874
00:41:20,920 --> 00:41:22,120
I want to give it a try.

875
00:41:23,180 --> 00:41:23,970
Thank you.

876
00:41:31,900 --> 00:41:32,800
Xia.

877
00:41:36,650 --> 00:41:37,320
Thank you.

878
00:41:37,320 --> 00:41:39,370
